Description: Code accompanying Alarid-Escudero et al. (2023)
    <doi:10.1177/0272989X221121747>, which shows how to implement
    simulation-time-dependent and state-residence-time-dependent cohort
    state-transition models (cSTMs) of the Sick-Sicker model in R and use them
    for a cost-effectiveness analysis, including transition rewards,
    within-cycle correction, probabilistic sensitivity analysis and
    epidemiological outcomes. This file records the project version and
    dependencies; the repository is not an installable R package.
